<span>=E2=9C=85 Architecture Answer:
</span></span><span>
</span><span>"WebSocket scaling involves several strategies:
</span><span>
</span><span>1. **Sticky Sessions**: Route connections to same server insta=
nce
</span><span>   - Use load balancer session affinity
</span><span>   - Store session info in shared store (Redis)
</span><span>
</span><span>2. **Message Broadcasting**:=20
</span><span>   - Use Redis Pub/Sub or message queues
</span><span>   - When user A sends message, server publishes to all instan=
ces
</span><span>   - Each instance broadcasts to its connected clients
</span><span>
</span><span>3. **Connection Distribution**:
</span><span>   - Use consistent hashing for deterministic routing
</span><span>   - Monitor connection counts per server
</span><span>   - Graceful server shutdown with connection migration
</span><span>
</span><span>4. **State Management**:
</span><span>   - Keep connection state in external store
</span><span>   - Share user presence info across instances
</span><span>   - Implement distributed locking for critical operations"</s=
pan></code></pre></div></div>
