Browser code is in <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bo=
rder-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px te=
xt-[0.9rem]">browser.js</code>.
Area of usage
Long polling works great in situations when messages are rare.
If messages come very often, then the chart of requesting-receiving message=
s, painted above, becomes saw-like.
Every message is a separate request, supplied with headers, authentication =
overhead, and so on.
So, in this case, another method is preferred, such as Websocket or Server =
Sent Events.</p></div></div><div class=3D"absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer=
