rection: ltr; text-align: left; white-space: pre-wrap; word-spacing: normal=
; word-break: normal; line-height: 1.5; tab-size: 2; hyphens: none;"><span>=
<span>=E2=9C=85 System design response:
</span></span><span>
</span><span>"Server architecture for resumable uploads requires several co=
mponents:
</span><span>
</span><span>**Upload State Management:**
</span><span>- Database table storing: fileId, userId, totalSize, uploadedB=
ytes, chunkMap
</span><span>- Redis cache for active upload sessions (faster access)
</span><span>- File system or object storage for actual chunk data
</span><span>
</span><span>**API Endpoints:**
</span><span>- POST /upload/initiate - Start new upload, return fileId
</span><span>- GET /upload/status/{fileId} - Return current upload progress
</span><span>- POST /upload/chunk/{fileId} - Upload individual chunk
</span><span>- DELETE /upload/{fileId} - Cancel v=C3=A0 cleanup upload
</span><span>
</span><span>**Chunk Storage Strategy:**
</span><span>- Temporary storage during upload (local disk or temp bucket)
</span><span>- Atomic file assembly after all chunks received
</span><span>- Cleanup job for abandoned uploads (TTL-based)
</span><span>
</span><span>**Concurrency Handling:**
</span><span>- File-level locking =C4=91=E1=BB=83 prevent concurrent chunk =
writes
</span><span>- Rate limiting per user (requests/minute, bandwidth/hour)
</span><span>- Load balancing v=E1=BB=9Bi sticky sessions or shared state
</span><span>
</span><span>**Data Integrity:**
</span><span>- Checksum validation for each chunk
</span><span>- Final file verification after assembly
</span><span>- Duplicate chunk detection v=C3=A0 handling
</span><span>
</span><span>**Monitoring:**
</span><span>- Active upload tracking
</span><span>- Storage utilization alerts =20
</span><span>- Performance metrics (upload speeds, error rates)
</span><span>- Cleanup job monitoring"</span></code></pre></div></div>
